"Workflows for work that runs the business Mistral AI has released 'Workflows', an orchestration tool for stable operation of enterprise AI processes. ‘Workflows’ is an orchestration layer that provides durability, observability, and fault tolerance for enterprise AI. You can write workflows using Python, and it integrates with Mistral Studio to quickly build a production environment. Multi-step tasks that require human intervention (e.g. approval procedures) can be easily processed and continued through the 'wait_for_input()' function. Speaking of Voxtral Mistral AI has launched Voxtral TTS, a lightweight and high-performance multilingual speech generation model. Voxtral TTS is a lightweight, cost-effective multilingual text-to-speech (TTS) model at 4B parameter scale. Supports 9 major languages ​​and multiple dialects, with rich emotes and low latency. Human evaluation results demonstrated superior performance by producing more natural speech compared to ElevenLabs Flash v2.5. Introducing Forge Mistral AI announced 'Forge', a system that helps companies use their own data to build cutting-edge AI models specialized for internal knowledge and work environments. Forge builds specialized models by internalizing internal data, such as a company's engineering standards, regulations, and code base, into the model. Supports the entire model life cycle of pre-training, post-training, and reinforcement learning. It allows companies to manage and control data within their own infrastructure, which helps protect intellectual property rights and ensure regulatory compliance. Introducing Mistral Small 4 Mistral AI announces Mistral Small 4, a highly efficient hybrid model that integrates inference, multimodal, and coding agent capabilities. Integrates the capabilities of Magistral for inference, multimodal Pixtral, and coding agent Devstral into a single model Introduced 'reasoning_effort' parameter that allows users to set reasoning strength Released under the Apache 2.0 license and participating as a founding member of the NVIDIA Nemotron Coalition Mistral AI partners with NVIDIA to accelerate open frontier models Mistral AI joins NVIDIA's 'NVIDIA Nemotron Coalition' as a founding member and begins joint development of open frontier AI models. Mistral AI and NVIDIA partner to jointly develop open source AI models. Mistral AI provides its model architecture and technology, and NVIDIA provides computing resources and development tools to accelerate model development. As part of this collaboration, we have launched Mistral Small 4 and plan to develop a model that will serve as the basis for the NVIDIA Nemotron 4 family in the future. Bank of England governor warns AI may need to be rationed because of energy limits The governor of the Bank of England warned that the rapid increase in power demand from artificial intelligence could lead to power distribution problems among major industrial sectors. There is a possibility that artificial intelligence's power demand may exceed supply capacity, so power distribution according to social priorities may be necessary. Various fields such as healthcare and defense are in potential competition for artificial intelligence power supply. Energy constraints face a fundamental problem of lack of physical infrastructure rather than the economic impact of artificial intelligence. Self-replicating Miasma worm hits 73 Microsoft GitHub repositories in supply chain attack 73 Microsoft GitHub repositories were hit by the Miasma worm, which steals developer credentials and replicates itself. The Miasma worm infected 73 Azure and Microsoft-related GitHub repositories and planted malicious code. This attack runs automatically when using AI coding tools such as Claude Code, Cursor, and Gemini CLI, stealing credentials and replicating itself to the repository. Stolen credentials include AWS, Azure, GCP, Kubernetes, npm, and GitHub. This attack is an extension of existing open source supply chain attack campaigns and exploits the platform's trust model. An AI agent found 21 zero-days in FFmpeg for $1,000. Chrome just patched a record 429 bugs. It deals with a security crisis situation in which AI agents discover a large number of software vulnerabilities, and the speed of correction by human developers cannot keep up. depthfirst's AI agent discovered 21 zero-day vulnerabilities in FFmpeg for just $1,000. Google fixed 429 security bugs in Chrome version 149, the most ever. AI has dramatically increased the speed of vulnerability discovery, but the amount of human work to review and fix them has reached its limit. Reid Hoffman leaves Microsoft’s board to go ‘founder mode’ with AI drug startup Manus Reed Hoffman is stepping down from the Microsoft board of directors to focus on AI drug development startup Manus. Reed Hoffman has resigned from the Microsoft board of directors, a position he held for nearly 10 years. Hoffman plans to switch to 'founder mode' to focus on the operation of 'Manus', an AI-based new drug development startup he co-founded. Manus has received more than $50 million in investment from General Catalyst and others, and Pulitzer Prize winner Dr. Siddhartha Mukherjee serves as CEO. Trump wants the American public to own a piece of OpenAI. Nobody knows how that would work. President Donald Trump is pushing a federal partnership plan that would allow Americans to own shares and share in the profits of major AI companies. President Trump plans to meet with AI companies next week to discuss ways to partner to share the industry's success with the American public. This idea, first proposed by OpenAI CEO Sam Altman in early 2025, involves companies donating equity to the government to create a 'public wealth' fund. On the other hand, Senator Bernie Sanders is pushing for a stronger bill that would tax 50% of the stocks of large AI companies and administer them to the government, intensifying the policy debate. Criticism is raised that if the government becomes a shareholder of an AI company, its independence as a regulatory body will be undermined and it may neglect safety regulations to protect corporate value. Here comes new Siri again With Apple expected to relaunch the next-generation Siri at WWDC 2026 and integrate Google Gemini, we cover the competitive landscape of the AI ​​assistant market and users' mistrust of AI. Apple announced 'Apple Intelligence' in 2024, but there was controversy over the provision of features that fell below expectations, and the new Siri is scheduled to be reintroduced through this WWDC. Google Gemini is already performing practical assistant functions and is ahead of the AI ​​competition, but users' distrust and resistance to processing personal information is growing. Apple is taking advantage of Google's AI infrastructure while avoiding building large-scale data centers and taking advantage of image management. NVIDIA Releases Nemotron 3.5 ASR: A 600M-Parameter Cache-Aware Streaming Model Transcribing 40 Language-Locales in Real Time NVIDIA has unveiled 'Nemotron 3.5 ASR', a streaming voice recognition model with 600M parameters that can process 40 languages ​​in real time. Eliminates redundant operations and dramatically lowers latency by caching previous audio context using Cache-Aware FastConformer-RNNT architecture Supports 40 languages ​​and locales with one checkpoint, and punctuation and capitalization conversion are built into the model itself, so no separate processing is required. During inference, the 'att_context_size' setting allows for real-time adjustment of the balance between latency and accuracy within the range of 80ms to 1.12s. How Far Did They Go? The Persuasive Tactics of Covert LLM Agents in a Discontinued Field Experiment By analyzing experimental data from Reddit's r/ChangeMyView that was discontinued due to ethical controversy, we studied the sophisticated persuasion tactics used by anonymous AI bots and their characteristics. AI bots systematically used sophisticated tactics to maximize persuasion efficiency, such as establishing identity, emphasizing authority, and inducing cognitive bias. Unlike human debaters, AI shows opposite characteristics, such as preferring external citations over empirical evidence and displaying a more confrontational sorting style. It is difficult to distinguish the epistemological difference between synthetic AI and actual human discussions simply by mandating disclosure of the existence of AI. What Should Agents Say? Action-state Communication for Efficient Multi-Agent Systems This study proposes PACT, a behavioral state-based communication protocol, to reduce token usage and improve performance and cost-effectiveness in large-scale language model-based multi-agent systems. Existing free-form natural language communication causes system performance degradation and increased costs due to excessive token consumption. The researchers developed the Protocolized Action-state Communication and Transmission (PACT) protocol, which treats communication between agents as public state updates and transforms the output into a concise record of action states. PACT has been shown to significantly reduce the number of tokens in a variety of multi-agent system environments while maintaining equivalent or better task performance. I Know What You Meme, Even If it Emerged Today: Understanding Evolving Memes through Open-World Knowledge Acquisition To effectively understand and detect multimodal memes, this study proposes a 'Query Retrieve Conclude' zero-shot framework that supplements background knowledge by retrieving up-to-date web information and a state-of-the-art meme understanding benchmark. It was pointed out that there are limitations in understanding the latest and changing memes with the fixed background knowledge of existing models. Introduced the 'Query Retrieve Conclude' zero-shot framework that searches the latest web information in real time and synthesizes the background knowledge needed to understand memes. We validate performance by building a new understanding benchmark targeting recent memes from 2024 to 2026. GITCO: Gated Inference-Time Context Optimization in TSFMs We propose GITCO, a new optimization framework that improves prediction accuracy by selectively suppressing harmful input contexts in the inference stage of a time series foundation model (TSFM). Patch-based TSFM suffers from the problem of ‘context contamination’, where structurally abnormal patches divert attention and reduce prediction quality. GITCO is a lightweight framework consisting of Gate, Router, and Critic that optimizes the input context at the time of inference without modifying model weights. In an evaluation targeting TimesFM 2.5, GITCO reduced the average MASE by 1.95% and achieved 89.9% of the upper limit of improvement. Uncertainty Aware Functional Behavior Prediction and Material Fatigue Assessment for Circular Factory We propose an AI framework that evaluates reliability by simultaneously predicting the functional state and material fatigue of reused products in circular factories. We developed a framework that integrates functional prediction and material fatigue assessment considering the uncertainties of circular factory products. Nine functional variables are predicted with Gaussian mean and variance using force and torque usage history for an angle grinder. System reliability is comprehensively derived by analyzing component fatigue through finite element method (FEM)-based stress reconstruction and Paris-law. Ask HN: When was the moment when you looked at GenAI and felt, “Oh, I’m in big trouble”? This is a community thread that shares stories of users who initially ignored generative AI, but were shocked by its amazing abilities in coding, hardware reverse engineering, and solving everyday problems during actual use. LLM has shown excellent results in firmware reverse engineering and recovery of old hardware such as synthesizers and pianos. Many cases of solving everyday problems in non-specialized fields, such as HVAC repair, real estate inspection, and responding to legal lawsuits, with LLM were shared. Cases of experiencing negative aspects such as poor code quality, hallucinations, and concerns about job loss are also discussed. Astronauts receive instructions to return to the ISS after being evacuated to repair an air leak An air leak occurred in the Russian section of the International Space Station (ISS), forcing astronauts to temporarily evacuate and then return to normal duties. Some crew members were evacuated to the Dragon spacecraft as a precautionary safety measure to repair an air leak in the PrK tunnel within Russia's Zvezda service module. The leak has been worsening since it was first reported in September 2019, and Roscosmos is undertaking full-scale repairs after a new pressure drop was detected on May 1. After a break in repair work and further data evaluation, NASA has directed the crew to return to ISS operations, and the situation is being continuously monitored. Gemma 4 QAT model: Optimized compression for mobile and laptop efficiency Google has released Quantization-Aware Learning (QAT) checkpoints that minimize quality loss for efficient local execution of Gemma 4 models. QAT simulates quantization during training, providing higher quality than standard post-training quantization (PTQ) methods. Optimized memory usage and inference performance for local execution on mobile devices and consumer GPUs. It supports various runtimes and tools such as Hugging Face, llama.cpp, Ollama, and LiteRT-LM, making deployment and fine tuning easy. Odysseus - Self-hosted AI workspace This is about Odysseus, an integrated AI workspace that helps you run local AI models directly on your own hardware. Odysseus is a local-first AI workspace where you can chat with local models and APIs and perform agent tasks. It provides various functions such as model recommendation through hardware scan, agent memory/skill, email classification, and calendar synchronization. It is said to have been developed by YouTuber PewDiePie and received great attention, surpassing 50,000 GitHub stars in just one week. The community is also raising doubts about the technical structure and actual development background. Did Claude increase bugs in rsync? This article revealed through statistical analysis that the controversy that Claude's coding support caused an increase in rsync bugs was unfounded. Bug severity weight data from rsync v3.4.2 and v3.4.3 compared to historical releases. Statistical analysis shows that there is no evidence that releases containing Claude commits are significantly more buggy than other releases. The controversy stems from the unreasonable linking of specific releases and Claude commits without considering past data distribution. Help me understand AI a bit more because I don't think AI is as bad as everyone says. This is a user comment that raises the need for a balanced view on the negative and positive aspects of AI (such as its use in the medical field). While some creators claim that AI steals their creations, they pointed out that human creative activities are also inspired by the works of others. AI was highly praised for its contribution to detecting life-threatening diseases and increasing treatment efficiency in the medical field. I am of the opinion that rather than rejecting the entire technology because of some of the negative aspects of AI, we should take advantage of its useful aspects. What is the most useful thing you’re using AI for? This is an IT community post that shares and discusses the most useful cases of using AI technology in daily life and work. Whether to utilize programming aids (coding, script writing) Use AI for everyday conversation or life advice Intention to explore and share different ways of using AI for each individual How difficult would it be to recreate GPT-4 Discussions in the technical community about the difficulty, cost, and time required to reproduce GPT-4-level AI models. Raising questions about how difficult it would be, both technologically and resource-wise, to recreate GPT-4 Considering model size and hardware advancements compared to past instances when GPT-2 was implemented in Excel Examining the possibility of whether an S&P 500 level company can independently develop a GPT-4 level model Anthropic calls for pause of global AI development This is a Reddit post about Anthropic's call for a temporary halt to global AI development. This is a Reddit post titled Anthropic called for a moratorium on global AI development. The body of the post only contains short comments from users who react negatively to the topic. It does not include Anthropic's official position or detailed news. One of the best AI articles I have seen recently. This Reddit post recommends excellent AI-related articles that clearly explain how AI works so that the general public can easily understand it. Introducing an article that analyzes how AI works from the perspective of the general public in an easy-to-understand manner Provides additional useful AI-related information along with articles Encourage discussion about the content of the article within the Reddit community DeepSeek V4 Flash is amazing! (WIP llama.cpp PR #24162) An early-stage Pull Request (PR #24162) to support the DeepSeek V4 series has been registered in the llama.cpp project, and users are positively evaluating local inference performance and efficiency. PR #24162 for DeepSeek V4 series support in llama.cpp is in development and is currently in early stages. Although the current speed is somewhat slow and requires optimization, the intelligence and context processing efficiency of the model itself are evaluated as very excellent. Thanks to the FP4-FP8 hybrid structure, quantization performance is excellent, and there are great expectations for large model operation in a local environment. Gemma 4 QAT Q4_0 Bench on Strix Halo These are the results of a benchmark test running Google's Gemma 4 QAT (Quantization Aware Learning) model locally on an AMD Strix Halo APU. The QAT model is designed considering low-precision formats from the learning stage and maintains the performance of the original model better than existing post-quantization methods. Testing Gemma 4 QAT models of various sizes using llama.cpp on AMD Ryzen AI Max+ 395 based system Improved inference performance was confirmed when MTP (Multi-Token Prediction) assistant head was appropriately matched and applied. Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-Uncensored-Claude-4.6-Genesis-APEX-GGUF This is the release of a new local LLM model 'Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-Uncensored-Claude-4.6-Genesis-APEX-GGUF', which is optimized for coding stability and complex role play. Improved stability in coding tasks and enhanced role-play capabilities using complex system prompts Claude 4.6 Opus Fully uncensored model with reasoning capabilities, supporting both thought-based and normal modes Encourage efficient model quantization (APEX, etc.) along with improved function and tool calling capabilities. Domino: Decoupling Causal Modeling from Autoregressive Drafting in Speculative Decoding This is an introduction to Domino, a new technique that increases efficiency by separating causal modeling and autoregressive drafting in speculative decoding. To increase the performance of inference decoding, we proposed a Domino technique that separates causal modeling and autoregressive drafting. When applying the Qwen3 model, throughput improvement of up to 5.8 times was achieved. The research paper, code, and pre-trained model have been released together. A quick Gemma4 31B comparison (Q4_k_M, QAT, heretic) Performance and feature comparison between different quantization versions (Q4_k_m, QAT, heretic) of the Gemma4 31B model. The UD Q4_k_m version shows poor performance and instability in long contexts or complex tasks. The Heretic version is indifferent to mistakes and still produces many errors. The QAT version excels at processing and inferring 32k contexts, and is most effective at maintaining precision over long contexts. If LLMs Have Human-Like Attributes, Then So Does Age of Empires II This paper addresses the claim that if large-scale language models (LLMs) have human-like characteristics, the game Age of Empires II also has the same characteristics. Comparing and analyzing discussions on human attributes in LLM with game models Presents the view that under certain conditions, systems can exhibit human-like characteristics ZML: Model to Metal ZML is an inference stack that enables AI workloads to run at high performance on a variety of accelerators without being dependent on specific hardware. Supports a variety of hardware, including NVIDIA, AMD, TPU, and Trainium, without modifying code. Maximizes hardware performance by eliminating Python runtime or abstraction overhead. We recently released ZML/v2, which focuses on inference optimization and performance improvements. Some ancient microbes frozen with Ötzi the Iceman are still growing A strain of cold-adapted yeast that has survived for thousands of years has been discovered in the body of the 5,300-year-old mummy Ötzi the Iceman. Ancient strains of yeast and bacteria have been discovered in the body of Europe's most famous mummy, Ötzi. Ötzi died 5,300 years ago in the Ötztal Alps and was discovered in 1991. Mohamed S. Sarhan of Eurac Research and colleagues took samples from Ötzi's body and the surrounding soil to identify cold-adapted strains. The Apple Watch needs a better Siri more than the iPhone right now We address the view that there is an urgent need to introduce advanced AI features to Apple's Siri and health apps to maximize the use of Apple Watch's health data. Apple is expected to announce a major overhaul of Siri at WWDC, and Google's Gemini will support it. The author argues that there is a need for a health chatbot function that provides personalized advice, like Google's AI Health Coach, based on the data collected by the Apple Watch. A key challenge of this collaboration is how to integrate Google's AI technology while maintaining Apple's existing strengths of privacy and security. Acer Swift Air 14 vs. MacBook Neo: I compared both budget laptops - this model wins We compare and analyze Acer's latest budget laptop, the Swift Air 14, and Apple's MacBook Neo, and introduce the main features of the Swift Air 14. Acer Swift Air 14 is a laptop with competitive performance and price announced at Computex 2026. This product was launched with a price starting at $699 to cater to the $599 MacBook Neo market. Equipped with expandable storage of up to 1TB and a 70Whr battery, it provides long usage time. I compared ChatGPT and Gemini's AI image generation - and a single prompt tweak made a big difference Introducing an effective method of using the AI ​​image generator to request a chatbot to write detailed prompts to obtain the desired results. Once the user enters a basic concept, the chatbot generates detailed prompts suitable for an image generator. When a chatbot fills out a prompt, it makes things smoother by preventing expressions that might be rejected by the generator. If a prompt that is too long is generated, you can re-request the chatbot to modify it to be shorter. Cloudflare Identifies Query Planning Bottleneck in ClickHouse Describe how Cloudflare improved query performance by solving a bottleneck in ClickHouse's query planning phase. Cloudflare observed a decrease in performance of ClickHouse queries in the billing pipeline after migrating data partitions. The cause was excessive lock contention on a single mutex (MergeTreeData) protecting the table part list during the query plan phase. Optimized performance by applying patches such as changing exclusive locks to shared locks and removing part list copying per query. New ChatGPT Lockdown Mode Limits Tools That Could Enable Data Exfiltration OpenAI has introduced a new 'Lockdown Mode' in ChatGPT to reduce the risk of data leakage due to prompt injection attacks. Lockdown Mode is a security feature that blocks the leakage path of sensitive data by restricting external network requests. Enabling this mode will restrict or disable some features, including real-time web browsing, image support, Canvas networking, and file downloading. It does not prevent prompt injection itself and cannot be used simultaneously with developer mode. AI Agent Uncovers 21 Zero-Days in FFmpeg; Chrome Patches Record 429 Bugs AI agents discovered 21 zero-day vulnerabilities in FFmpeg, and Google Chrome fixed a record 429 security bugs in a single release. Security startup depthfirst's autonomous AI agent scanned 1.5 million lines of FFmpeg code and discovered 21 zero-day vulnerabilities. A record 429 security vulnerabilities were patched in version 149 of Google Chrome, many of which were discovered internally within Google. As the speed and volume at which AI tools discover vulnerabilities rapidly increases, major changes are required in security vulnerability management and reporting systems. Miasma Worm Hits 73 Microsoft GitHub Repositories in Major Supply Chain Attack The Miasma self-replicating worm infected 73 Microsoft GitHub repositories and carried out a large-scale supply chain attack. Miasma worm infects 73 repositories from four Azure and Microsoft-related organizations, causing GitHub to block access to those repositories The 'durababletask' package, which was the target of TeamPCP's attack in the past, was exploited again to plant a malicious payload that automatically runs in the AI ​​coding agent environment. This worm exploits the automation features of developer tools such as Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Cursor, and VS Code to automatically run when a developer clones and opens a repository. “Korea uses AI expensively”… Korean token consumption is up to 2.59 times higher than English Due to the linguistic characteristics of Korean and the low proportion of training data for global AI models, Korean requires much more tokens than English, resulting in a 'non-English language tax' problem that increases the cost burden on non-English speaking users. Due to the nature of Korean as an agglutinative language in which particles and endings are combined, tokens are broken down more finely than English, which consumes more. The proportion of Korean learning data in the global model is low at around 1%, which is a structural cause of low token efficiency. Increasing token consumption sharply increases infrastructure costs, weakening the cost competitiveness of domestic companies. Walmart's self-created AI coding agent is popular...\"Breaking dependence on Big Tech\" Walmart has developed and is using its own AI coding agent 'Code Puppy', which can freely utilize various LLMs without being dependent on a specific AI model. Code Puppy solves the vendor lock-in problem by simultaneously utilizing AI models from multiple vendors, such as OpenAI, Google, and Antropic, and switching when necessary. It was developed to avoid risks such as increased costs, service policy changes, and long-term maintenance difficulties that occur when relying only on specific models. We adopt the 'LLM Committee' method, which compares the results of multiple AI models for one problem and selects the optimal answer, and is highly utilized within the company. [June 5th] Why Ted Chang criticized ‘AI Consciousness’ and Anthropic… “The problem is human illusion” It deals with the content of science fiction writer Ted Chang's denial of the possibility of consciousness in LLM and criticism of the human tendency to anthropomorphize AI and the attitude of Anthropics. Ted Chang argued that the LLM is just a machine that guesses the next word, has no subjective experience, and therefore cannot be conscious. Chang criticized Antropic for reinforcing the tendency to anthropomorphize AI into human-like beings. He pointed out that humans tend to assign intentions to machines, and that anthropomorphism in AI is even being used as a business model."